    "https://www.whittier.edu/humanresources/faculty#assistant-professor-of-economics": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Economics",
      "description": "The Department of Economics at Whittier College seeks applications for a tenure-track appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning in Fall 2027. The department seeks a macroeconomist with teaching and research interests in development economics and multidimensional poverty. Preference will be given to candidates whose scholarship employs applied empirical methods and who can contribute to the department’s quantitative curriculum. The successful candidate will teach six courses per year: one section of ECON 300 Intermediate Macroeconomic Theory, three sections of ECON 200 Principles of Macroeconomics, and two upper-division electives in monetary economics, development economics, or the candidate’s specialty. These courses serve Economics majors and minors as well as students in several other programs, and the position may also involve contributions to quantitative methods, interdisciplinary programs, and general education. Candidates should demonstrate a strong commitment to inclusive and effective undergraduate teaching in a liberal arts setting. The College particularly values candidates who can engage students in applied research, supervise undergraduate research and senior projects, and involve students in faculty scholarship as research assistants or coauthors. Candidates should hold a Ph.D. in Economics by the time of appointment. Evidence of teaching effectiveness and the potential to maintain a productive scholarly program are required. The position also carries responsibilities for academic advising, departmental governance, College service, and participation in the broader intellectual life of the Whittier College community. Tenure Status: Tenure Track Exempt Status: Exempt Full Time/Part Time status: Full-time Salary Range: $90,000 annually; salary will commensurate with experience, skills, and knowledge. Reports to: Vice President Academic Affairs Location/Department: Whittier College / Economics Position Requirements Candidates should hold a Ph.D. in Economics by the time of appointment. Evidence of teaching effectiveness and the potential to maintain a productive scholarly program are required. The position also carries responsibilities for academic advising, departmental governance, College service, and participation in the broader intellectual life of the Whittier College community. Application Deadline November 15, 2026 Application Materials Applicants should submit a letter of application describing their relevant teaching and mentoring experience, other relevant qualifications, and work authorization status; a curriculum vitae; a job market paper; a statement of teaching philosophy; a statement of research interests; a graduate transcript; and three letters of reference. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Submit application materials to econsearch@whittier.edu . Direct questions regarding this advertisement to rwhite1@whittier.edu."
    },
    "https://www.whittier.edu/humanresources/faculty#assistant-professor-of-history": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of History",
      "description": "Whittier College invites applications for a tenure track assistant professor in the Department of History. The Department of History at Whittier College seeks a colleague for a tenure-track, open-rank position in United States history, covering any period from the colonial era to the present. We particularly welcome applicants who specialize in African American or Native American history, or who study the histories of Latino and/or Asian American populations.  Individuals who work on the historical intersections of race, class, gender, sexuality, and/or other identity categories are especially encouraged to apply, as are candidates who bring depth and expertise in new or emerging fields, including environmental history and public history. A successful candidate will develop introductory as well as upper-division courses in areas that reflect their interests and will also participate in teaching departmental seminars and contribute to Whittier’s Liberal Education program. We seek a colleague with a clear commitment to engaging with undergraduates from a wide range of racial, class, gender, cultural, linguistic, and economic backgrounds, and who wants to teach in a liberal arts setting, which means smaller classes, close academic mentoring of students, and continuous assessment and improvement of our teaching. Individuals with a history of, and commitment to, teaching and mentoring students from underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply. We also seek someone who is interested in collaboratively honing the curriculum of Whittier’s history major and, since faculty at Whittier College are also scholars, who has an ongoing and promising research agenda in their area of specialization and interest. Tenure Status: Tenure Track Exempt Status: Exempt Full Time/Part Time status: Full-time Salary Range: $80,000-$85,000 annually; salary will commensurate with experience, skills, and knowledge. Reports to: Vice President Academic Affairs Location/Department: Whittier College / History Position Requirements Successful candidates will have their Ph.D. in hand by August 2027. Candidates with extensive teaching experience as instructors are especially welcome. Application Deadline December 31, 2026 Applicants should submit a letter of application (which describes relevant teaching and mentoring experiences, the dissertation and/or the most recent scholarly project, as well as other appropriate experiences), a statement of teaching philosophy, a CV, a graduate transcript, and two letters of reference. Review of materials will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Submit application materials to historysearch@whittier.edu. Direct questions regarding this advertisement to jorozco@whittier.edu."
    },
    "https://www.whittier.edu/humanresources/faculty#assistant-professor-of-kinesiology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Kinesiology",
      "description": "Whittier College invites applications for a tenure track assistant professor in the Department of Kinesiology, specializing in motor learning and control, beginning work in August 2027. The Department of Kinesiology seeks an outstanding candidate whose experience in teaching, research, or community service has prepared them to contribute to our commitment to educating a diverse body of students. The faculty member will have the opportunity to teach undergraduate courses on motor learning and control, research methods/statistics, courses that contribute to the liberal arts curriculum, and selected courses in kinesiology at the introductory and advanced levels.  In addition, the successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to supervise senior seminar projects and lead undergraduate research in motor learning and control. Whittier College prides itself on inclusive, hands-on teaching of undergraduates and engagement with students in undergraduate research. The faculty member will also help advise students and engage in service work for the college. Tenure Status: Tenure Track Exempt Status: Exempt Full Time/Part Time status: Full-time Salary: $80,000 annually; Salary will commensurate with experience, skills, and knowledge. Reports to: Vice President Academic Affairs Location/Department: Whittier College / Kinesiology Position Requirements Applicants are expected to have completed a Ph.D. in Kinesiology with a focus on motor learning and control, or a closely-related field with specialization in motor learning and control, by August 2027 Successful teaching experience Shows potential of a successful research agenda Effective communication skills Application Deadline Applicants should submit a letter of application, which describes relevant teaching and mentoring experiences, the dissertation and/or the most recent scholarly project, as well as other appropriate experiences, a statement of teaching philosophy, a c.v., a graduate transcript, and two letters of reference. Review of materials will begin immediately, and will continue until the position is filled. Submit application materials to knssearch@whittier.edu. Direct questions regarding this advertisement to mhouseholder@whittier.edu . Whittier College is committed to attracting and retaining a high quality, diverse faculty with a shared passion for student-centered teaching and mentoring. Distinguished by small class sizes, high-impact pedagogies, and an innovative liberal arts curriculum, it is a nationally recognized model for inclusion and diversity. With over 65% students of color, Whittier is both an HSI and AANAPISI. Founded in 1887, it is an independent, four-year liberal arts college with about 1,700 undergraduates, ideally situated in the scenic hills 18 miles east of downtown Los Angeles. Whittier College is an Affirmative Action, Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate against employees or applicants because of race, religion creed, color, national origin, ancestry, physical disability, mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, age, or sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by State or Federal Law. Faculty Opportunities Breadcrumb Home / Human Resources / Faculty Opportunities Human Resources Expand Human Resources Menu Human Resources Employment at Whittier Expand Employment at Whittier Menu Administrative and Support Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Student Employment Expand Student Employment Menu FAQs Student Employee Handbook Supervisor Information Forms Employee Benefits Expand Employee Benefits Menu Benefits Portal Policies & Information Holiday Schedule Contact Us Footer Consumer Information Employment Terms of Use Whittier College is committed to ensuring the accessibility of its web content to people with disabilities. We strive to meet W3C WAI’s Web Content Accessibility Guidelines 2.0, Level AA conformance. To report an accessibility issue, a website problem, or submit feedback, please submit a Website Feedback Form . Copyright © 2026 Whittier College 13406 E. Philadelphia St. Whittier, CA 90602 562.907.4200 Give Visit Apply Request Info window.addEventListener('load', function(){\n\tif(window.location.pathname == \"/admission/closeconfirmation\"){\n\tgtag('event', 'conversion', {'send_to': 'AW-761719594/j8DYCMma7r8BEKrWm-sC'});\n  }\n  if(window.location.pathname == \"/gradrficonfirmation\"){\n\tgtag('event', 'conversion', {'send_to': 'AW-761719594/edenCObU2s0BEKrWm-sC'});\n  }\n}); {\"path\":{\"baseUrl\":\"\\/\",\"pathPrefix\":\"\",\"currentPath\":\"node\\/128\",\"currentPathIsAdmin\":false,\"isFront\":false,\"currentLanguage\":\"en\"},\"pluralDelimiter\":\"\\u0003\",\"suppressDeprecationErrors\":true,\"ajaxTrustedUrl\":{\"\\/directory\\/search\":true,\"\\/search\\/google\":true},\"googlePSE\":{\"language\":\"en\",\"displayWatermark\":false},\"user\":{\"uid\":0,\"permissionsHash\":\"26758c5dd6132cc2807a8f1bcfacb04e6ed7f8ff6fdd0571812cbea9a2a460a8\"}} /*<![CDATA[*/\n\t\t\t\t\t\t(function () {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tvar sz = document.createElement('script');\n\t\t\t\t\t\tsz.type = 'text/javascript';\n\t\t\t\t\t\tsz.async = true;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tsz.src = '//siteimproveanalytics.com/js/siteanalyze_66357412.js';\n\t\t\t\t\t\tvar s = document.getElementsByTagName('script')[0];\n\t\t\t\t\t\ts.parentNode.insertBefore(sz, s);\n\t\t\t\t\t\t})();\n\t\t\t\t\t/*]]>*/ Google Tag Manager (noscript) End Google Tag Manager (noscript)"
